{"contract":"rgp-pems2-admission-transaction/2","expected_base_sha256":"3e7ea8f0e2c89bd313923fac96ce5729f7c74654a296b575cc356b26cde83e36","new_records":[{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted install-package contract makes manifest content identity the semantic identity of installed package content and verifies the SHA-256 of exact archive transport bytes separately."},"id":"pems:proposition:1429c6189decbce4202e5cce","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a31a5af7b7ff3a8e7d2d6551"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted installer-runner contract defines `rd_install.py` as a deterministic network-independent Python 3 CLI that consumes local package files, an expected transport digest, and an explicit project target while leaving package retrieval and release selection to the runner."},"id":"pems:proposition:1906ff6fd7e170de0ece854b","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65999f0c9355338334bbe4d8"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The P8 release baseline defines accepted immutable release publication as a package, manifest, transport digest, installer, package validator, and schemas tied to an exact source commit and content identity."},"id":"pems:proposition:1d8a0a7ae541986a41aa8b81","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:677737dfdbcd178e65ee5b02"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The consumer-migration record states that migration must preserve project-owned knowledge and authority while replacing cross-repository runtime coupling with the project-local installed framework."},"id":"pems:proposition:2ff19e1cee25bd589bd72584","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:84c95a06bad51dacbb72ed2a"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The install-package final plan records the accepted distribution model as an immutable versioned local package retrieved by an authorized runner and installed with deterministic `rd_install.py`, rather than cross-repository runtime coupling."},"id":"pems:proposition:42fbb1326d303c5d6f10870e","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65b03f079de0b86b50f154e3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted install-package contract states that compatibility metadata declares what the package can work with but does not grant authority or select an active backend for a project."},"id":"pems:proposition:43ace07192a09840a1a4c682","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a31a5af7b7ff3a8e7d2d6551"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The install-package final plan defines update as installation of another verified package through the same installer transaction, removing old files only when the prior verified manifest proves package ownership and leaving unmanaged files untouched."},"id":"pems:proposition:55dadf3dc71e91818d7e90e0","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65b03f079de0b86b50f154e3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The install-package final plan defines a failure/recovery pressure suite covering bad transport, manifest mismatch, traversal or duplicate paths, incompatible project/backend state, managed drift, interrupted activation or restore, same-version different-content identity, missing runtime files, and source-repository unavailability."},"id":"pems:proposition:58e4bef13920b5b1bfa67f97","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65b03f079de0b86b50f154e3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The P7 update-proof record demonstrates a second package-version update through the same installer mechanism with an auditable managed-tree diff rather than a separate updater implementation."},"id":"pems:proposition:6003199c9ac38262bed0242c","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:fbc5b8c115c8a77ac98ef15a"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted installer-runner contract excludes current network state, mutable repository heads, implicit version discovery, environment-specific source paths, and current time from the inputs allowed to determine installed framework content."},"id":"pems:proposition:666b382431f8983f36f94d5a","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65999f0c9355338334bbe4d8"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The current release-status record reports PASS for Reasoning Distiller v0.5.2, source commit `90bc23ed90f12f06d41d019c79994747709ab326`, content identity `sha256:db4afb76e9cf1ae6abcc837a74bb26aa290528672bbfee5a9fa6839f48121c24`, and transport SHA-256 `e83814c2ff050fb63f609c1738e1d8ebdf1adbf196e32f2dd8d17796f7bb3ca3`."},"id":"pems:proposition:943a993a2cddd8a926047472","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:22c5506d165f915f37fc6d5c"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The install-package final plan requires installed runtime and already-retrieved installer execution to remain functional with the source repository unavailable and network access disabled, with no remote fallback for missing runtime files."},"id":"pems:proposition:a0ef33099c52f4467ec49dfd","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65b03f079de0b86b50f154e3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted install-package contract requires manifest paths to remain normalized, unique, relative, non-escaping package paths and excludes symlink package entries in v1."},"id":"pems:proposition:aa51bee7116ea441497f1813","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a31a5af7b7ff3a8e7d2d6551"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The current release-status record identifies `reasoning-distiller-project/2` as the project contract and records `semantic_authority_changed` as false for v0.5.2."},"id":"pems:proposition:aabc16545335b3b97da83330","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:22c5506d165f915f37fc6d5c"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The final install-package plan states that package updates do not silently migrate canonical project knowledge and that integrity, compatibility, drift, and recovery failures fail closed."},"id":"pems:proposition:be004b0619addb722a57e886","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65b03f079de0b86b50f154e3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted installer-runner contract requires managed-file drift, unsafe archive paths, manifest disagreement, and project-owned path mutation attempts to fail closed."},"id":"pems:proposition:c1971132607d0e795f4cfd94","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65999f0c9355338334bbe4d8"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted install-package contract requires successful installations to persist the exact verified release manifest and an installation record containing release, content, transport, source, installer, and compatibility metadata while keeping operational event metadata outside package content identity."},"id":"pems:proposition:c7573f56fc5f65faaffb1947","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a31a5af7b7ff3a8e7d2d6551"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The final install-package plan states that packaging or installing a generic Steward role definition does not grant Steward authority in a consuming project and that executor/installer mechanics do not acquire semantic authority."},"id":"pems:proposition:c85862532c77d0b39ca5a04d","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65b03f079de0b86b50f154e3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The install-package final plan requires the package builder to use an explicit generic-framework allowlist instead of packaging the repository wholesale, and excludes project-specific canonical state, authority, activation, and integration material."},"id":"pems:proposition:c9e5d1fde41ae6cf3cd76017","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65b03f079de0b86b50f154e3"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The runtime-isolation record states that P5 proves installed runtime and installer operation do not require network access or a live generic source checkout after package retrieval."},"id":"pems:proposition:d76ba547bbbf04b7aedf63d1","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:44ea21e62737762851211e84"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The deterministic-builder record describes P2 as an allowlisted reproducible builder whose clean builds must yield the same canonical manifest/content identity and reject excluded or unsafe content."},"id":"pems:proposition:da35ad2b9e62e24eb9d723f2","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:873c8424ecde35b2cc2e5f49"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The journaled-recovery record describes P4 recovery as restoration or completion from durable local transaction state so interrupted installation does not leave an indeterminate managed tree."},"id":"pems:proposition:df9d02ee8d856ebc1b6384de","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a57d5165fc2b1f61f974c5a4"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The deterministic-installer record describes P3 as a staged local installer transaction with integrity checks, compatibility checks, managed-drift detection, idempotent repeat behavior, and deterministic update behavior."},"id":"pems:proposition:e435199c3b509bd657b9d041","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:345a8e02856ccacbd91ac9d5"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The accepted installer-runner contract restricts installer mutation to the declared managed root and transaction/recovery material; project knowledge, canonical state, authority, policy, evidence, adapters, integration, and role activation are not installer-owned."},"id":"pems:proposition:f8428d11730f4423ebe5aa49","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:65999f0c9355338334bbe4d8"]}},{"data":{"authority":"repository_state","identity_locator":{"path":"docs/packaging/P2_DETERMINISTIC_BUILDER.md","repository":"loteque/reasoning-distiller"},"source_kind":"repository_file"},"id":"pems:source:2e520f31211314e6ba3fc024","kind":"source","lifecycle":"current"},{"data":